phase 6.7/runner evidence closure:
- Replaced the resolution runner's seven-case SUPPORTED early exit with explicit profiles for all 20 declared names.
- Added real runner coverage for idempotent Resolve, direct pre-handshake fallback, replay rejection, ticket-byte binding rejection, expiry rejection, sequential reuse, and 64 concurrent opens; these cases assert event cardinality, fingerprints, stream uniqueness, and selected-path order.
- Added explicit missing-evidence failures for binding matrix completion, revision mutation, resolve/proxy limits, exchange/server restart, and graceful-drain instead of silently certifying generic authorization.
- Fixed the runner privacy marker list to avoid treating public case labels as secrets while retaining token/raw-ticket/session/private-selector scans.
